<title>USA: AT&amp;T to end year with same size work force - WSJ.</title>
<headline>AT&amp;T to end year with same size work force - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>While AT&amp;T eliminated about 7,700 jobs during the year, the cuts were mostly offset by hiring in the company's fast-growing wireless, Internet, customer care and local phone operations, The Wall Street Journal reported Monday.</p>
<p>The company will end 1996 with about the same number of workers as a year ago, despite being vilified earlier this year for planning to cut thousands of employees, the story said.</p>
<p>&quot;We've been downsizing with one hand and upsizing with the other,&quot; a company spokesman was quoted as saying.</p>
